NetHack 5.0.1 for Nintendo 3DS
==============================

Install
-------
Copy the contents of the "nethack" folder in this package to
    sdmc:/3ds/nethack/
on the 3DS SD card, and copy NetHack3ds.3dsx anywhere the Homebrew
Launcher can see it (e.g. sdmc:/3ds/NetHack3ds.3dsx).  The game keeps
its data files (nhdat, sysconf, record, save files, bones, ...) in
sdmc:/3ds/nethack, so that folder must be writable.

Play
----
Launch the Homebrew Loader and start NetHack3ds.

The bottom screen is the control surface: the libctru console shows
messages and menus, the D-pad walks (hjkl), L+pad runs, A/B/X/Y are
rest/inventory/grab/search, START saves, SELECT opens help, and touch
brings up the button keyboard for prompts and menus.

The top screen renders the map in stereoscopic 3D: push the 3DS 3D
slider up and the level becomes a diorama -- walls sit at the glass,
monsters and objects a little behind, furniture (altars, up stairs)
raised, floors deeper still, and down stairs deepest of all; a
levitating or flying hero drifts up to its own plane.  Slider down
gives the flat picture.  Diagnostics go to sdmc:/3ds/nethack/nh3ds.log.

Building from source
--------------------
See sys/unix/README.hints ("CROSS_TO_3DS") and sys/3ds/PLAN.md.
